³1version³21³2ts³21098021022³2ip³265.219.208.102³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= Where can I get PGP/<nowiki>GnuPG</nowiki> for my computer? =

PGP can be downloaded free for non-commercial use from the net at [http://www.pgpi.org/products/pgp/versions/freeware/ The International PGP Home Page]:

Freeware PGP versions

:Amiga (8)
:Atari (6)
:<nowiki>BeOS</nowiki> (5)
:EPOC (Psion etc.)
:<nowiki>MacOS</nowiki> (22)
:MS-DOS (9)
:Newton
:OS/2 (6)
:<nowiki>PalmOS</nowiki> (2)
:Unix (19)
:Windows 2000 (5)
:Windows 3.x (2)
:Windows 95/98/NT (31)
:Windows ME (3)
:Windows XP (4)

GPG is on most or all distributions. If you have a Linux installation, it is most likely there, already installed or waiting on the installation CDs. Check your distribution help files or in the terminal window type "pgp --help" or "gpg --help". If it's there, you will get the program's help page.
